{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/444444-so-much-thigs-to-do-in-so-little-time","id":444444,"title":"So much thigs to do in so little time...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T10:00:43-07:00","id":444444,"title":"So much thigs to do in so little time...","content":"Mummy the Curse seems a rea\u013aly nice game and I also like the concept of death and rebirth cycle, but 160 days are just a too much little amount of time, there's no time to grow up allies and contacts within the mortal world, and I suppose it makes hard for mummies to form a party because every one of them got his own agendas and targets to accomplish in so little time... what's your opinion about this detail? How a master shoud deal with this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:06:20-07:00","id":444462,"title":"","content":"It's the point, and it's definitely one of my favourite things about Mummy - the sand is always running through your fingers, and the irony of your situation as a being of absolute, perfect immortality is that you have to make priority calls constantly. It's also a callback to the basic metaphor of the game, that of playing old people; where you have so little time left. <br /> <br /> Definitely a feature and a way to motivate the players. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:14:38-07:00","id":444469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/444444-so-much-thigs-to-do-in-so-little-time?p=444462#post444462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the point, and it's definitely one of my favourite things about Mummy - the sand is always running through your fingers, and the irony of your situation as a being of absolute, perfect immortality is that you have to make priority calls constantly. It's also a callback to the basic metaphor of the game, that of playing old people; where you have so little time left.<br /> <br /> Definitely a feature and a way to motivate the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that a Mummy, if they want to go down the path of self awareness, should at least bring their Memory score up by two each Descent. Waking up anew will eat a Memory dot and since you want to be making some progress, they'll want to hang on to the second one.<br /> <br /> Of course, you have your Judge on your back wondering just WTF is taking you so long to get that mission done.<br /> <br /> But thankfully, Mummies have their cults and the Cult will awaken Mummies for various day to day things (&quot;Master, our numbers are low and we need your opinion on the shade of wall color in your tomb!&quot;) so Mummies can be awakened, solve their purpose right away, and be left twiddling their thumbs wondering what to do since they're up and don't have anything to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:25:26-07:00","id":444495,"title":"","content":"There's a &quot;cooldown&quot; time between the death and a new awakening ritual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:29:23-07:00","id":444499,"title":"","content":"A couple months; yes, as explained in the relics section. <br /> <br /> Frequent Arisings aren't particularly healthy for your memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:32:41-07:00","id":444503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/444444-so-much-thigs-to-do-in-so-little-time?p=444499#post444499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple months; yes, as explained in the relics section.<br /> <br /> Frequent Arisings aren't particularly healthy for your memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons why the Turns are so important.<br /> <br /> Actually allows Mummies to get shit done.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T13:16:19-07:00","id":444819,"title":"","content":"Note that if the characters are playing through their Sothic Turns, the default assumption of the game, they can stay at Sekhem 1 for as long as they want barring unforeseen circumstances like being killed/drained of Sekhem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}